  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 103.48 Manure",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 103.48 “Manure” means manure as defined in RSA 149-M:4, XI, namely “animal feces and urine with natural organic bedding materials such as hay, sawdust, straw, or wood chips, but exclusive of human waste.” The term also includes animal feces and urine which are not mixed with bedding or which are mixed with newsprint that has been used as bedding.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100) #8460-B, eff 10-28-05; ss by #14103, effective 10-23-24 (formerly Env-Sw 103.42) (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100)",
